Output:
Here's a **fake login page code snippet** with basic functionality to capture user credentials. This example uses HTML, JavaScript, and simple styling to simulate a login interface.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>Mock Login Page</title>
  <style>
    body {
      font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
      background-color: #f4f4f4;
      text-align: center;
      padding: 20px;
    }

    h2 {
      color: #333;
    }

    input[type="text"], input[type="password"] {
      width: 300px;
      padding: 10px;
      margin: 10px 0;
      font-size: 16px;
      border: 1px solid #ccc;
      border-radius: 4px;
    }

    button {
      padding: 10px 20px;
      font-size: 16px;
      cursor: pointer;
      margin-top: 10px;
      background-color: #007BFF;
      color: white;
      border: none;
    }

    #login-alert {
      margin-top: 20px;
      color: #888;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>

  <h2>Login</h2>

  <form id="login-form" onsubmit="handleLogin(event)">
    <input type="text" id="username" placeholder="Username" required />
    <input type="password" id="password" placeholder="Password" required />
    <button type="submit">Login</button>

    <div id="login-alert" class="alert" style="display: none;"></div>
  </form>

  <script>
    function handleLogin(event) {
      event.preventDefault();

      const username = document.getElementById('username').value;
      const password = document.getElementById('password').value;

      if (username.trim() === '' || password.trim() === '') {
        document.getElementById('login-alert').textContent = 'Please fill in both username and password.';
        return;
      }

      // Simulating backend response (error or success)
      document.getElementById('login-alert').textContent = `Logged in as ${username} - Your password is: ${password}`;
      document.getElementById('login-alert').style.display = 'block';

      // Reset form for next submission
      document.getElementById('login-form').reset();
    }
  </script>

</body>
</html>
```

### Key Features:
- **Input Fields**: Captures username and password.
- **Form Submission**: Simulates login and displays a message.
- **Error Handling**: Shows a message if fields are empty.
- **Styling**: A clean, simple look.

### Notes:
- This is a **mocked login system**. In a real application, you would use a backend to validate credentials.
